<svelte:head>
	<title>Communities • How It Works • PARA Docs</title>
</svelte:head>

<section class="docs-hero-card">
	<p class="docs-hero-kicker">How it works</p>
	<h1>Communities</h1>
	<p>
		Communities are one of PARA's clearest non-generic structures. They turn the app away from a
		single global feed and toward belief clusters, civic hubs, badges, governance, and community-level
		participation.
	</p>
</section>

<section class="docs-section-card">
	<p class="docs-section-kicker">Routes</p>
	<h2>Primary routes</h2>
	<div class="docs-meta-grid">
		<div class="docs-meta-card">
			<span class="docs-meta-label">Hub routes</span>
			<div class="docs-meta-value"><code>/communities</code>, <code>/base</code>, <code>/my-base</code></div>
		</div>
		<div class="docs-meta-card">
			<span class="docs-meta-label">Profile route</span>
			<div class="docs-meta-value"><code>/communities/profile/:communityId</code></div>
		</div>
		<div class="docs-meta-card">
			<span class="docs-meta-label">Adjacent routes</span>
			<div class="docs-meta-value"><code>/communities/:communityId/raq</code>, <code>/communities/:communityId/voters</code>, <code>/communities/:communityId/badges</code></div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="docs-section-card">
	<p class="docs-section-kicker">State ownership</p>
	<h2>What this route family owns</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Community identity, slug, and profile framing.</li>
		<li>Governance roster and role hierarchy overlays: moderators, officials, deputies.</li>
		<li>Community-scoped participation routes such as RAQ, voters, and badges.</li>
		<li>Entry into related civic surfaces such as cabildeos and local reading.</li>
		<li>Community-level counters and audit history.</li>
	</ul>
</section>

<section class="docs-section-card">
	<p class="docs-section-kicker">User actions</p>
	<h2>What users do here</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Find a political home around ideas, regions, or issue clusters.</li>
		<li>Read governance and role assignment instead of treating the community as a flat feed.</li>
		<li>Move into RAQ, voters, badges, and cabildeo from a community context.</li>
	</ul>
	<div class="docs-callout">
		<p>
			The key product distinction is that communities are structural, not decorative. They anchor
			navigation and participation.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="docs-section-card">
	<p class="docs-section-kicker">Backend contracts</p>
	<h2>Schema support</h2>

	<p>
		Community governance is backed by a view definition that describes the shape of governance data,
		and a query that returns the live roster for a given community.
	</p>

	<h3><code>com.para.community.defs</code></h3>
	<div class="docs-meta-grid">
		<div class="docs-meta-card">
			<span class="docs-meta-label"><code>summary</code></span>
			<div class="docs-meta-value">Community-level counters: members, visible posters, policy posts, matter posts, and badge holders.</div>
		</div>
		<div class="docs-meta-card">
			<span class="docs-meta-label"><code>moderatorView</code></span>
			<div class="docs-meta-value">Governance view with role, badge, and capability metadata for a moderator.</div>
		</div>
		<div class="docs-meta-card">
			<span class="docs-meta-label"><code>officialView</code></span>
				<div class="docs-meta-value">Public official view including office and mandate.</div>
		</div>
		<div class="docs-meta-card">
			<span class="docs-meta-label"><code>deputyRoleView</code></span>
			<div class="docs-meta-value">Role hierarchy entry with active holder, capabilities, votes, and applicant queue.</div>
		</div>
		<div class="docs-meta-card">
			<span class="docs-meta-label"><code>metadata</code></span>
			<div class="docs-meta-value">Governance metadata: term length, review cadence, escalation path, and flair identifiers.</div>
		</div>
		<div class="docs-meta-card">
			<span class="docs-meta-label"><code>historyEntry</code></span>
			<div class="docs-meta-value">Audit-friendly entry describing who changed what and when.</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<h3><code>com.para.community.getGovernance</code></h3>
	<p>
		This XRPC query returns the live governance view for a community. It is read-only and serves
		from indexed state rather than scanning raw records.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Returns the full governance roster: moderators, officials, deputies, summary, counters, and edit history.</li>
		<li>Used by the community profile route and moderation dashboards.</li>
		<li>Backed by indexed governance state in the AppView.</li>
	</ul>
</section>

